<!--
  Inbox — AndroidManifest.xml additions
  =======================================
  Merge these snippets into your existing AndroidManifest.xml.

  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  1. PERMISSIONS — add inside <manifest> alongside existing permissions
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->

<!--
  READ_CALL_LOG — reads recent call history from CallLog.Calls.
  Separated from READ_CONTACTS since Android 9 (API 28).
  Classified as a dangerous permission; requested at runtime in InboxFragment.
  Google Play requires a declaration in the Play Console Data Safety section.
-->
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_CALL_LOG" />

<!--
  READ_SMS — reads the SMS database via Telephony.Sms.
  Dangerous permission; requested at runtime.
  Note: apps that only read SMS for their own use-case may need to apply
  for the SMS permission via Play Console's Permissions Declaration Form.
  EZ Launcher reads SMS purely to display a simplified inbox — no sending,
  no data upload, no third-party sharing.
-->
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_SMS" />

<!--
  READ_CONTACTS — already added for Speed Dial; included here for reference.
  SmsReader.resolveContact() uses ContactsContract.PhoneLookup to resolve
  SMS sender addresses to display names and photos.
-->
<!-- <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.READ_CONTACTS" /> -->

<!--
  CALL_PHONE — already added for SOS and Speed Dial; included here for reference.
  InboxViewModel.onCallTapped() uses ACTION_CALL to dial back.
-->
<!-- <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CALL_PHONE" /> -->

<!--
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  2. GOOGLE PLAY — Data Safety section (required declarations)
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  EZ Launcher uses the following data in the Data Safety form:
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Data type            │ Collected? │ Shared? │ Required? │ Purpose        │
  ├──────────────────────┼────────────┼─────────┼───────────┼────────────────┤
  │ Phone number (calls) │ No         │ No      │ Optional  │ App feature    │
  │ SMS messages         │ No         │ No      │ Optional  │ App feature    │
  │ Contacts             │ No         │ No      │ Optional  │ App feature    │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  Data is read on-device only — never uploaded, stored on a server, or shared
  with third parties. This must be declared honestly in Play Console.

  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  3. PROGUARD — add to proguard-rules.pro
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  # Keep Telephony constants used by SmsReader
  -keep class android.provider.Telephony { *; }
  -keep class android.provider.CallLog { *; }
-->
